1. Identify the superclass and subclasses.

The superclass is Employee. The subclasses are FullTimeEmployee, PartTimeEmployee, and Manager.

2. Explain how inheritance reduces code duplication.

Inheritance allows subclasses to reuse common fields and methods from the Employee class instead of writing the same code repeatedly.

3. Identify the method that demonstrates polymorphism.

The calculateSalary() method demonstrates polymorphism because each subclass provides its own implementation. The Employee[] array allows different employee objects to be processed using the same parent type.

4. Explain why @Override is used.

@Override indicates that a subclass is redefining a method inherited from its parent class. It also helps the compiler detect mistakes in the method signature.